+Hit-tracker request bytes require no separate metric: `sum(rate(buildbuddy_proxy_remote_bytes{method="hit_tracker.HitTrackerService/Track",direction="sent"}[5m]))` includes synchronous and batched Track RPCs. The existing Track histogram's `_sum` counts hits in batches, while `_count` counts requests; it did not count serialized bytes.
+
+The fraction of AC local hits that still went remote is `sum(rate(buildbuddy_proxy_action_cache_revalidations[5m])) / (sum(rate(buildbuddy_proxy_action_cache_revalidations[5m])) + sum(rate(buildbuddy_proxy_action_cache_read_requests{result_source="ttl_fast_path"}[5m])))`, for normal remote-authoritative requests. Inspect the `changed` and `error` outcomes separately before choosing a TTL; the age histogram is conditional on changed results and available metadata, not a survival curve for all local entries.
+
+# Integration with behavior tasks
+
+No sibling agents or branches named `proxy-splitblob` or `proxy-partial-read` were available in this workspace. The shared ByteStream edits are limited to recording the final read outcome, incrementing partial-read miss count, and recording whether an attempted read-through local write committed. SplitBlob detection lives in the stats handler, so moving the local lookup ahead of SplitBlob requires no added hook. The partial-read behavior task should retain the final read-outcome counter and emit commit observations only when it actually attempts a local write; skipped writes should not count as failures. AC TTL behavior already present in the checkout is preserved.
+
+The stats handler covers the default app connection, opt-in routing connections, and the hit-tracker connection. Routing registration accepts optional dial options so the proxy can install the observer without changing other routing users. Background atime updates use the observed CAS client, so their RPCs and bytes are also included, normally with `not_checked`. The existing atime request counter isolates those background calls from foreground FindMissingBlobs traffic.
+
+# Validation
+
+Added tests for inclusive reuse windows, same-request duplicates, refresh semantics, bounded LRU eviction, isolation, concurrent access, final-outcome attribution, remote byte accounting, mixed-compressor batch payloads, bounded method labels, and streaming sampling limits/partial-read exclusions, successful complete-blob sampling, and AC revalidation outcomes/age including ignored metadata errors and the default-off lookup behavior. Proxy integration tests also verify exact RPC and byte attribution for cached GetTree with an all-local batch followed by partial-hit and miss batches, encryption-bypass remote errors, SplitBlob NotFound followed by a successful local read, and real partial-read local writes that commit or fail validation. All six test targets passed uncached; the touched libraries and cache proxy binary built successfully, including required nogo static analysis.
+
+```sh
+bazel test --nocache_test_results \
+  //enterprise/server/util/proxy_util:all \
+  //enterprise/server/byte_stream_server_proxy:all \
+  //enterprise/server/content_addressable_storage_server_proxy:all \
+  //enterprise/server/action_cache_server_proxy:all \
+  //enterprise/server/capabilities_server_proxy:all \
+  //enterprise/server/ocifetcher_server_proxy:all \
+  //enterprise/server/hit_tracker_client:all \
+  //enterprise/server/cmd/cache_proxy:all \
+  //enterprise/server/routing/routing_service:all \
+  //server/metrics:all
+```
+
+[Bazel invocation](https://app.buildbuddy.io/invocation/4ab65adc-a14c-4efc-af71-4a2dcf246272). `git diff --check` also passes.
